From 22b4fc7d1172f1daf97c6fc58b1d4892fa1cf287 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:44:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: fix fdm_rate for Alyx's headset render paths

Serialise rate map creation and use across recording threads, and only
rebuild a map when the captured density data changes.

Lay the rate map out at the 32 pixel density texel size instead of
stretching the density map over the framebuffer, so maps sized to a
smaller render area land where the application expects.

Give each map version its own parameter block, and update an image's
block with a GPU copy recorded before the render pass that uses the map,
so work recorded earlier still decodes with the map it rendered with.

Carry the view's base layer and the image's own size in the sampled
image descriptor for coordinate mapping, and map texel fetches of
subsampled images. Input attachments keep physical coordinates.

KK_FDM_DEBUG=1 logs density uploads, pass setups and how subsampled
images are used.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

